## 🔐 Security Settings

### Firestore Security Rules
Location: `firestore.rules`

All read/write operations require authentication:
```javascript
rules_version = '2';
service cloud.firestore {
  match /databases/{database}/documents {
    match {
      match /{document=**} {
        allow read, write: if request.auth != null;
      }
    }
  }
}
```

### Firebase Authentication
- Email + OTP verification enabled
- No anonymous authentication
- Email provider configured

---

## 📊 Performance Targets

| Metric | Target | Threshold |
|--------|--------|-----------|
| App cold start | < 2 seconds | Warning > 3s |
| Screen transitions | 60 FPS | Warning < 55 FPS |
| API response time | < 500ms | Warning > 1s |
| Bundle size | < 30 MB | Warning > 50 MB |

---

## 🧪 Testing Standards

### Coverage Requirements
- **Critical paths:** ≥ 90% coverage
- **Business logic:** ≥ 80% coverage
- **UI components:** ≥ 70% coverage

### Test Types Priority
1. Unit tests (business logic, validators)
2. Widget tests (components, forms)
3. Integration tests (user flows)
4. E2E tests (critical paths only)

---

## 🚀 Deployment Settings

### Build Configuration

**Production Builds:**
- Release mode only
- Minify code enabled
- Obfuscate symbols enabled
- Stripe/Firebase production keys

**Debug Builds:**
- Development mode
- Logging enabled
- Hot reload available

### App Store Requirements
- iOS 12.0+ (minimum)
- Android API 21+ (minimum)
- Privacy policy URL required
- Terms of service URL required

